We arrive at the park.
There are a lot of people here today.
Other dogs are also there.
Bruno sniffs a tree with interest.
He pulls a bit, but I hold him tightly.
We slowly keep walking.
Suddenly, Bruno sees a squirrel.
The squirrel is sitting in front of the bushes.
Bruno immediately starts running.
He barks loudly and wants to go into the bushes.
I quickly pull on the lead.
"Stop!"
"Stay here!" I call strictly.
Bruno stops in surprise.
He looks at the small animal.
Then he looks at me.
Sabine's rule is really important.
He must stay on the lead in the park.
I pet him briefly and we keep walking.
